message: "If you use this software, please cite the repository and the associated manuscript."
title: "RSNA ICH Multi-Window Explainable Deep Learning Pipeline"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sekkat"
    given-names: "Hamza"
    affiliation: "Hassan First University of Settat"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/HamzaSekkat-AI/rsna-ich-multiwindow-xai"
url: "https://github.com/HamzaSekkat-AI/rsna-ich-multiwindow-xai"
abstract: >-
  A DICOM-native, multi-window deep learning and explainability pipeline for
  multi-label detection of intracranial hemorrhage subtypes on non-contrast
  head CT. The repository includes DICOM-to-Hounsfield-unit conversion,
  brain, subdural, and bone window construction, patient- and study-aware
  cross-validation, ResNet34 training, validation-derived threshold
  optimization, performance evaluation, and explainability analyses using
  Grad-CAM, Integrated Gradients, occlusion sensitivity, window ablation,
  and deletion-insertion faithfulness assessment.
keywords:
  - intracranial hemorrhage
  - head CT
  - deep learning
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - DICOM
  - ResNet34
  - medical imaging
